<title>POLAND: POLISH STOCKS CLOSE HIGHER IN CONTINUOUS TRADE.</title>
<headline>POLISH STOCKS CLOSE HIGHER IN CONTINUOUS TRADE.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve stocks rose, two fell and seven were flat in 30.5-million-zloty Warsaw bourse continuous trade on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The WIG 20 index closed at 1,665.8 points, 0.6 percent higher than at the regular session.</p>
<p>The remaining two stocks did not trade.</p>
<p>NFI units fell 0.3 percent to 147 zlotys in a 12.9-million-zloty turnover.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
